\f1\fs22 As the last embers of the barbecue settled into a warm glow and background conversations hummed, the sound of a car door slamming broke through the evening calm. A looming tension poured in alongside Chilo, who appeared in his usual eccentric robes\'97but to the collective surprise of everyone, he was not alone. The Johnny followed in his shadow, confidently adorned in a casually flashy suit that seemed wholly incongruous with the Chuglinghams\'92 suburban domesticity. His presence demanded attention as though the aura of his own importance had arrived ahead of him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo\'92s lateness elicited a collective raised eyebrow from the Sages, not least from Kleoboulos, who motioned impatiently to his empty wrist as if to ask, "What time is this?" Chilo answered with his characteristic flourish, bowing slightly and offering his hands palm-up in mock solemnity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I must apologize for our tardiness. The Travelator, naturally\'97well, failed. As it does,\'94 he said gracefully, ignoring everyone\'92s knowing groans. \'93Think of it not as a flaw in punctuality, but in relativity itself. Punctuality is a construct as mutable as temporal variance, which, I should add, is entirely subjective unless you\'92ve done the maths.\'94 His explanation drew an exasperated sigh from Kleoboulos.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah, who had been perched near Kathy on the edge of the fire pit, stood to take control of the interaction. "And Johnny? What\'92s his excuse?" she asked bluntly enough to cut through any charming masquerade.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Johnny waved broadly as though planning to embrace everyone at once. "How could I resist, Sarah? I heard there\'92d be\'85 barbecue? And family fun? Isn\'92t that just delightful?" His grin dripped insincerity, but coupled with his undeniable electricity, no one could quite figure out how to rebuff him. "Besides," he added, gently steering the conversation sideways, "Chilo wouldn\'92t stop insisting I come along and, really, I\'92m just here to soak up the ambience. After all," he gestured to Bala expertly wrangling a particularly defiant grill grate, "who am I to turn down the chance to witness masterful domesticity in action?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Bala, torn between pride at the comment and indignation at the patronizing tone, responded with a neutral grunt.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny breezed forward to Padmala with a theatrical bow. "Madam," he said, affecting an archaic formality, "what a glorious event you\'92re hosting. For such warmth of spirit, you must allow me to offer a small token of appreciation." He produced a bottle of wine with an illegibly ornate label, handing it over with such energy that Padmala was left momentarily nonplussed, cradling the gift like an unwelcome relic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy exchanged a glance with Sarah that seemed to articulate the unspoken: Why is he here again?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny circled back toward the now-united group of Sages and addressed the lot in that half-inspirational, half-obtuse tone he had perfected: "You know, the cosmos has a strange sense of humor. Here I am, surrounded by individuals of such remarkable purpose. And here we are at a barbecue! Can you imagine the parallels between the charred edges of a particularly stubborn steak and\'85 say, the outermost frequencies of universal gravitational constants?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Johnny,\'94 Kleoboulos interrupted, his voice steady with the authority of having completely had enough. \'93You\'92re late because Chilo invited you?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo coughed to cover his facial wince as Johnny preened, answering for himself: "Well, of course. Who else could spark even temporal inefficiencies into brilliance?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stepped forward, pointing directly at the bottle Padmala still held awkwardly. "Is that meant to compel everyone here to forget your theatrical interruption?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny turned to Padmala, suddenly solemn. "That? Nah. That\'92s just wine. Thought maybe your husband could grill it, too."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The entire group groaned practically in unison, but Johnny\'92s smile persisted as though he had missed the point. Even Bala cracked into reluctant laughter, caught between his own annoyance and the irrepressible Johnny charm.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo, in the meantime, began carefully examining the fire pit embers as though they contained coded wisdom, leaving the Johnny to his verbal tap dance with the gathered crowd. Within minutes, the group\'92s mood softened into amused exasperation, and while no one quite trusted him, the Johnny\'92s deference to Padmala\'92s barbecue acumen won him some slim measure of tolerance for the remainder of the evening.
